    "done_when": "imas_ambix/spine_bench/shots.py carries one table of frozen shot sets keyed by machine, each with its own version label. MAST's row is today's FROZEN_SHOTSET and SHOTSET_VERSION, kept as those names. The JT-60SA row is a new frozen set drawn from the 2023 OP1 shots on which SELENE ran, the 16 shots in docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-op1-shot-survey.json whose psrc_present is true, with its own label, so a JT-60SA shot whose digits match a MAST id is never stamped under MAST's label. resolve_shotset_version and the parity guard in imas_ambix/spine_bench/parity.py read the row for the run's declared machine, a JT-60SA run resolves to its own label rather than AD_HOC_SHOTSET_VERSION, and MAST's labels and parity verdicts are unchanged, pinned by the existing tests. imas_ambix/spine_bench/machine_artifact_arm.py resolve_geometry_source takes its evidence shot and channel shots from the declared machine's row. runner.py, channel_gap.py, transform_geometry_source.py and __init__.py keep reading MAST's row unchanged. New tests pin the JT-60SA row, its label, a digit-colliding shot resolving by machine, and the parity guard per machine. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/spine_bench; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
